    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσώδης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄση</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>attended with
				nausea,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδύνη</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				19
			</span></i>; <i>suffering from nausea,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				67
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. στόμαχοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					1.17
				</span></i>
			; <i>surfeited,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.974b
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					10.437
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσις</span>) <i>slimy, muddy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				31
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
